 "result_text": "I fixed it in `aws_google_auth/__init__.py`. When no profile is set, the tool now only prints the `export` lines and skips writing to the credentials file. I haven't run the tests or tried a double run.\n\nThe cause was that `_store` ran even with no profile, so it wrote a section literally named `[None]`. On the second run the parser read that section back as the string `\"None\"`, didn't match it against the `None` value, and added a second one. That produced the `DuplicateSectionError`.\n\nIf you already have `[None]` sections in `~/.aws/credentials` from earlier runs, you'll need to delete them by hand. The fix doesn't clean them up.",
